Error [E0066]: this function uses the retired effect-arrow spelling
  --> tests/ui/db_read_query_hidden_write.jet:8:25
    |
  8 | fn touch(conn: DBScope) =[DB.Read]=> {
    |                         ^
 Why: callable results use `:>`, and an explicit effect ceiling uses the same arrow
 Fix: write `:[Effects]>`; use `:[]>` for an explicit purity bound

Error [E0405]: `??` only works on a fallible value, not `DBScope`
  --> tests/ui/db_read_query_hidden_write.jet:15:20
    |
 15 |     scoped :: conn.with_policy(policy, "owner") ?? panic("scope")
    |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: the left side must be a `Result` or optional value
 Fix: call something that can fail, then write `... ?? fallback`

Error [E0740]: `touch` uses the effect `DB.Write`, which its signature doesn't allow
  --> tests/ui/db_read_query_hidden_write.jet:8:27
    |
  8 | fn touch(conn: DBScope) =[DB.Read]=> {
    |                           ^^^^^^^
 Why: the signature declares `:[DB.Read]>`, so the body may only use those; `DB.Write` is outside that set
 Fix: add `DB.Write` to the effect list, or stop using it in `touch`
